{"name":"Candy Heart Pink","hex":"#f5a2a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Crystallized sugar formed by boiling down sugar syrup.","Edible, sweet-tasting confectionery containing sugar, or sometimes artificial sweeteners, and often flavored with fruit, chocolate, nuts, herbs and spices, or artificial flavors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook in or coat with sugar syrup.","To form into congelations or crystals, especially of sugar or syrup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candy"},{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweethearts (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweethearts are small heart-shaped sugar candies sold around Valentine's Day. Each heart is printed with a message such as \"Be Mine\", \"Kiss Me\", \"Call Me\", \"Let's Get Busy\", \"Miss You\", or \"I'm Yours\". Sweethearts were made by the New England Confectionery Company, or Necco, before being purchased by the Spangler Candy Company in 2018. They were also previously made by the Stark Candy Company. Necco manufactured nearly 8 billion Sweethearts per year. Similar products are available from Brach's and other companies. A similar type of candy is sold in the UK under the name Love Hearts; while similar in formulation to Sweethearts, Love Hearts are round, with the heart design and message embossed on their surface."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/Necco-Sweethearts-Box-Small.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweethearts_(candy)","wikidata":"Q7655713"},{"title":"Candy","blocks":[{"text":"Candy, also known as sweets and lollies, is a confection that features sugar as a principal ingredient. The category, sugar confectionery, encompasses any sweet confection, including chocolate or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/330px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy","wikidata":"Q185583"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Necco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg/500px-Necco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Necco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg/1280px-Necco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Necco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg/500px-Necco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Necco Sweethearts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANecco-Candy-SweetHearts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Candylol.jpg/500px-Candylol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Candylol.jpg/1280px-Candylol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Candylol.jpg/500px-Candylol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Sweetheart with the phrase \"LOL\", a relatively new phrase","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACandylol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Shop%22_from_Akizato_Rito%27s_Miyako_meisho_zue_%281787%29.jpg/500px-Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Sh